  "track": "track-09",
  "title": "incident response on-call and post-incident learning",
  "status": "source-backed-draft-generation-enabled",
  "concepts": [
    "Incident response reduces user harm while preserving a shared understanding of impact, current actions, and decision ownership.",
    "An incident is declared and classified using customer impact and urgency; severity labels are local policy, not universal standards. A commander coordinates work while technical leads investigate and communicators keep stakeholders informed.",
    "Containment and service restoration usually precede full root-cause analysis. Mitigation may be reversible and temporary; recovery is confirmed with service indicators rather than assumed from a successful deploy.",
    "A post-incident review reconstructs contributing conditions and system defenses without assigning blame. Actions should have an owner, measurable completion criteria, and priority proportional to risk.",
    "On-call systems need actionable alerts, escalation paths, runbooks, access, and sustainable rotation design. Automation reduces toil only when its failure modes and rollback are understood."
  ],
